@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-applypatch-rejects-sparse-patch-arrays-and-undefined-values
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch rejects sparse patch arrays and undefined values"
+status: pending
+---
+
+# Context
+
+RFC 6902 requires a patch to be an array of operation objects, and `value` to be a JSON value.
+`applyPatch` iterated with `forEach` (skips holes) and only checked that a `value` member existed.
+
+# Decision
+
+- Iterate operations by index so every slot is validated; a hole is an invalid operation and throws.
+- A `value` of `undefined` counts as missing (it is not a JSON value); `null` stays valid.
+- Refines dl-002 ("missing `value`" invalid); no other behaviour changes.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- Callers passing hand-built patches with holes or `undefined` values now get an error instead of a
+  silently wrong result.
